    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d600-a2">

                <pb facs="1054" n="954" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg954"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 229. </seg><dateline
                        rendition="#float-right">Extract from the Gazette de
                            <placeName>Lausanne</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-11-24">November 24,
                    1879</date></dateline>.—Translation.</opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">swiss abroad.</hi></head>
                <p>Several complaints having been addressed to the Federal Council, in order that an
                    end might be put to the active propaganda of Mormon agents in Switzerland, the
                    Federal Council has decided that there is no occasion for them to take special
                    measures, inasmuch as the cantonal laws punish polygamy, and that the American
                    Government, in execution of the act of Congress of July 1, 1862, seeks to
                    completely suppress it in the Territory of Utah. The Federal Council declares,
                    moreover, that last summer,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d600-f1"/> it intervened upon
                    the request of a family to reclaim a young girl who had emigrated at the
                    instigation of a Morman agent.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d600-f1" n="*" xml:id="d600-f1-content">
                <p>In the German text the words “last summer” are made to qualify the date of
                    emigration.—N. F.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
